# Findings the `Secret scan` job may skip, by fingerprint.
#
# A fingerprint is `commit:path:rule:line`, so an entry here silences exactly
# one match in one commit -- not the rule, not the file. That is the point: the
# same rule firing on a real key somewhere else still goes red.
#
# Only add a line here for something that is genuinely not a credential. A
# credential that *was* committed is not silenced, it is rotated: the commit is
# what GitHub serves, so removing it from the tip changes nothing.
#
